{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":191662,"duration_api_ms":213803,"num_turns":29,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"892cecc7-05d8-4082-b123-0b959b9b4e5e","total_cost_usd":1.2427161000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":1686,"cache_creation_input_tokens":75924,"cache_read_input_tokens":963209,"output_tokens":5764,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":75924,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1686,"outputTokens":5764,"cacheReadInputTokens":963209,"cacheCreationInputTokens":75924,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1086595000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":104,"outputTokens":5621,"cacheReadInputTokens":524001,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42758,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.13405659999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the provenance schema (tank_core::types::provenance) and its integration into the preset loader (tank_data::presets). The core ParamMeta schema is well-designed: strict ConfidenceLevel enum, optional fields with serde defaults for backward compatibility, deny_unknown_fields, range checking, and a clean display formatter. Tests cover the six acceptance criteria. However, I found several correctness and consistency issues: (1) a dual-schema inconsistency where the preset-level Provenance struct accepts freeform strings for confidence while per-parameter ParamMeta validates strictly, (2) NaN silently passes range checks due to IEEE 754 semantics, and (3) no validation that valid_range bounds are well-ordered.","amendments":[{"body":"In check_param_range (provenance.rs:116-127), NaN values silently pass the range check because IEEE 754 comparisons with NaN always return false. Add a !value.is_finite() guard that produces a RangeWarning (or a distinct diagnostic) when the value is NaN or infinity, and add a test for this edge case.","rationale":"The rest of the codebase actively guards against NaN (invariants.rs has many is_finite checks). A NaN value slipping through a range check undetected contradicts the purpose of the check and could mask simulation corruption. This is especially important since the acceptance criteria says 'out-of-range values produce a warning or similarly explicit diagnostic path.'"},{"body":"The preset-level Provenance struct (presets.rs:14-19) uses confidence: Option<String>, allowing arbitrary strings like 'medium' (present in shipped TOML files default.toml:99 and soft_acidic.toml:23). The per-parameter ParamMeta uses the validated ConfidenceLevel enum. Either: (a) change Provenance.confidence to Option<ConfidenceLevel> and update the shipped TOML files to use valid enum values, or (b) document the intentional difference and add a note explaining that preset-level confidence is freeform while per-parameter confidence is validated.","rationale":"Having two confidence fields with the same name but different validation semantics is confusing and error-prone. A developer seeing confidence = 'medium' in the TOML may assume 'medium' is a valid confidence level for ParamMeta, leading to load failures. The acceptance criteria calls for confidence-level validation, which the preset-level path does not perform."},{"body":"Add validation that valid_range[0] <= valid_range[1] during deserialization or in check_param_range. An inverted range like [5.0, 0.1] would cause every value to trigger a spurious warning. A simple assertion or early return with a descriptive warning would prevent silent misconfiguration.","rationale":"There is no guard against inverted ranges. Since valid_range is [f64; 2] with no semantic constraint, a typo like valid_range = [5.0, 0.1] would silently invert the check and generate false warnings for every in-range value."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"29a46b86-41ec-43e4-bb6d-b9cae26614e8"}
